1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:03,549
An actuator that fails without warning grounds an aircraft.

2
00:00:03,549 --> 00:00:05,644
AcuMain gives the maintenance planner

3
00:00:05,644 --> 00:00:08,080
a reviewed action list before that happens.

4
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:11,426
The planner brings in diagnostic records.

5
00:00:11,426 --> 00:00:13,849
Here it is the organisers' test file:

6
00:00:13,849 --> 00:00:15,355
2,000 actuator records.

7
00:00:16,526 --> 00:00:18,258
A team of agents takes over.

8
00:00:18,258 --> 00:00:21,537
The orchestrator hands the records to the Risk agent,

9
00:00:21,537 --> 00:00:24,383
which calls our trained Stage 2 failure model.

10
00:00:24,383 --> 00:00:27,785
The 25 most urgent aircraft move onto this week's list.

11
00:00:27,785 --> 00:00:31,497
The Stock agent takes spare actuators from the hangar store,

12
00:00:31,497 --> 00:00:34,405
and the Supply agent requests the missing ones.

13
00:00:34,405 --> 00:00:36,323
Stock and supply are simulated.

14
00:00:38,298 --> 00:00:40,639
The result: 203 of 2,000 actuators

15
00:00:40,639 --> 00:00:42,980
are likely to fail within 30 days.

16
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,630
Each repair comes with its reason and its spare part,

17
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:49,178
and some parts would arrive too late.

18
00:00:49,512 --> 00:00:51,304
Open any aircraft to see why.

19
00:00:51,304 --> 00:00:54,394
The hologram shows its nose landing gear actuator,

20
00:00:54,394 --> 00:00:56,866
drawn from this aircraft's own readings:

21
00:00:56,866 --> 00:00:58,472
fluid leaking at the seal,

22
00:00:58,472 --> 00:01:01,501
and the gear swinging slower than a new actuator.

23
00:01:02,544 --> 00:01:05,056
Nothing happens until a person decides.

24
00:01:05,056 --> 00:01:08,729
The planner sees the risk, the reason and the spare part.

25
00:01:08,729 --> 00:01:11,241
Approve creates a simulated work order.

26
00:01:11,241 --> 00:01:12,916
Reject asks: are you sure?

27
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:15,365
And any decision can be changed later.

28
00:01:16,231 --> 00:01:17,989
A blank reading is not hidden.

29
00:01:17,989 --> 00:01:21,741
With the leakage reading blank, the aircraft is still predicted,

30
00:01:21,741 --> 00:01:23,676
and marked as reduced confidence.

31
00:01:27,308 --> 00:01:30,473
With both key readings blank, there is no prediction:

32
00:01:30,473 --> 00:01:32,385
the team proposes a repeat test.

33
00:01:32,910 --> 00:01:36,160
If the failure model does not answer, the review stops.

34
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:38,819
Nothing is proposed, and nothing is invented.

35
00:01:42,562 --> 00:01:45,002
Once the model is back, the planner tries again,

36
00:01:45,002 --> 00:01:46,274
and the review completes.

37
00:01:50,534 --> 00:01:54,585
Every decision and every tool call is kept in the activity log,

38
00:01:54,585 --> 00:01:56,643
with its exact input and output.

39
00:01:56,643 --> 00:01:59,409
A work order exists only after an approval.

40
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:03,904
On aircraft it never saw, the model flagged

41
00:02:03,904 --> 00:02:07,729
185 of 187 failures, typically 5 weeks ahead.

42
00:02:07,729 --> 00:02:10,874
AcuMain runs from one Docker command.
